<title>USA: US chain store leading indicator up 0.5 pct Nov 23.</title>
<headline>US chain store leading indicator up 0.5 pct Nov 23.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi/Chain Store Age weekly leading indicator of U.S. chain store sales rose 0.5 percent in the week ended November 23 from the prior week, according to a Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi report.</p>
<p>It had risen 0.3 percent the week before, the report said.</p>
<p>The indicator was up 1.2 percent year-over-year, compared with a 0.7 percent increase the previous week, it said.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
